1
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:04,840
It's the end of the

2
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:05,790
year.

3
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:06,950
The rainy season should be

4
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:07,850
here.

5
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:09,270
So why does Singapore still

6
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:10,743
feel like an oven?

7
00:00:10,743 --> 00:00:12,688
My fur is melting!

8
00:00:12,688 --> 00:00:13,878
My water bowl went down

9
00:00:13,878 --> 00:00:14,947
again.

10
00:00:14,947 --> 00:00:15,537
I feel great,

11
00:00:15,537 --> 00:00:16,557
actually.

12
00:00:16,557 --> 00:00:18,266
Lizards love the heat!

13
00:00:18,266 --> 00:00:19,476
Not us!

14
00:00:19,476 --> 00:00:20,766
Drink lots of water and

15
00:00:20,766 --> 00:00:22,506
stay in the shade.

16
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:24,608
The answer starts thousands of

17
00:00:24,608 --> 00:00:25,918
kilometres away,

18
00:00:25,918 --> 00:00:27,748
over the Pacific Ocean.

19
00:00:27,748 --> 00:00:28,868
Let's shrink down and go

20
00:00:28,868 --> 00:00:29,958
there.

21
00:00:30,202 --> 00:00:31,462
Are you ready?

22
00:00:31,462 --> 00:00:32,502
Three!

23
00:00:32,502 --> 00:00:33,492
Two!

24
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:34,492
One!

25
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:35,652
Go!

26
00:00:40,093 --> 00:00:40,943
You are a gust of

27
00:00:40,943 --> 00:00:42,133
wind.

28
00:00:42,313 --> 00:00:43,523
You blow over the Pacific

29
00:00:43,523 --> 00:00:45,413
Ocean from east to west,

30
00:00:45,413 --> 00:00:47,073
day after day.

31
00:00:47,223 --> 00:00:48,383
People call you the trade

32
00:00:48,383 --> 00:00:49,653
wind.

33
00:00:49,899 --> 00:00:50,599
Below you,

34
00:00:50,599 --> 00:00:52,279
the sea is warm.

35
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:53,669
You push the warm top

36
00:00:53,669 --> 00:00:54,879
layer of water along with

37
00:00:54,879 --> 00:00:55,459
you,

38
00:00:55,459 --> 00:00:56,159
west,

39
00:00:56,159 --> 00:00:57,929
towards Singapore.

40
00:00:58,165 --> 00:00:59,495
The warm water gains heat

41
00:00:59,495 --> 00:01:00,925
from the Sun.

42
00:01:01,095 --> 00:01:02,515
Some of it evaporates into

43
00:01:02,515 --> 00:01:04,435
water vapour and rises with

44
00:01:04,435 --> 00:01:05,395
you.

45
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:06,185
High up,

46
00:01:06,185 --> 00:01:08,345
the water vapour loses heat,

47
00:01:08,345 --> 00:01:10,625
condenses into tiny water droplets

48
00:01:10,625 --> 00:01:12,555
and forms clouds.

49
00:01:12,807 --> 00:01:13,977
Over Singapore,

50
00:01:13,977 --> 00:01:16,026
the clouds rain down.

51
00:01:16,177 --> 00:01:18,317
That is a normal year.

52
00:01:19,159 --> 00:01:20,079
But this year,

53
00:01:20,079 --> 00:01:22,259
you grow weaker and weaker.

54
00:01:22,469 --> 00:01:24,009
The warm water slides back

55
00:01:24,009 --> 00:01:24,789
east,

56
00:01:24,789 --> 00:01:26,719
away from Singapore.

57
00:01:26,859 --> 00:01:27,529
The warm,

58
00:01:27,529 --> 00:01:28,949
wet air that rises from

59
00:01:28,949 --> 00:01:29,489
it,

60
00:01:29,489 --> 00:01:31,189
and builds the rain clouds,

61
00:01:31,189 --> 00:01:32,779
moves east too.

62
00:01:32,779 --> 00:01:33,419
Wait for us,

63
00:01:33,419 --> 00:01:34,909
clouds!

64
00:01:35,145 --> 00:01:37,455
You look down at Singapore.

65
00:01:37,635 --> 00:01:39,155
Blue sky.

66
00:01:39,345 --> 00:01:41,635
Hardly any rain clouds.

67
00:01:41,805 --> 00:01:42,745
What you just lived through

68
00:01:42,745 --> 00:01:45,235
has a name: El Niño.

69
00:01:46,273 --> 00:01:47,753
On the twelfth of November,

70
00:01:47,753 --> 00:01:49,113
scientists at NOAA in the

71
00:01:49,113 --> 00:01:51,033
USA said this El Niño

72
00:01:51,033 --> 00:01:53,003
is strong to very strong.

73
00:01:53,003 --> 00:01:53,753
Back in May,

74
00:01:53,753 --> 00:01:55,663
Singapore's weather scientists had already

75
00:01:55,663 --> 00:01:57,593
warned us: a warmer,

76
00:01:57,593 --> 00:01:59,883
drier June to October.

77
00:02:00,131 --> 00:02:01,481
The middle of the Pacific

78
00:02:01,481 --> 00:02:03,431
is more than 2 degrees Celsius

79
00:02:03,431 --> 00:02:05,001
warmer than usual.

80
00:02:05,001 --> 00:02:06,331
When it gets that warm,

81
00:02:06,331 --> 00:02:07,781
scientists call it a Super

82
00:02:07,781 --> 00:02:08,986
El Niño.

83
00:02:08,986 --> 00:02:10,813
Only 2 degrees?

84
00:02:10,813 --> 00:02:12,323
Across a whole ocean,

85
00:02:12,323 --> 00:02:13,503
that is a huge amount

86
00:02:13,503 --> 00:02:14,683
of heat.

87
00:02:15,531 --> 00:02:17,361
Let's name what you saw.

88
00:02:17,361 --> 00:02:19,341
Water gains heat and evaporates

89
00:02:19,341 --> 00:02:21,091
to form water vapour.

90
00:02:21,091 --> 00:02:23,051
When water vapour loses heat,

91
00:02:23,051 --> 00:02:25,441
it changes into water droplets.

92
00:02:25,441 --> 00:02:28,051
This process is called condensation,

93
00:02:28,051 --> 00:02:29,071
where a change in state

94
00:02:29,071 --> 00:02:31,521
from gas to liquid occurs.

95
00:02:31,521 --> 00:02:33,551
The droplets fall as rain.

96
00:02:33,551 --> 00:02:35,191
The continuous movement of water

97
00:02:35,191 --> 00:02:36,021
from the Earth to the

98
00:02:36,021 --> 00:02:37,561
sky and back to the

99
00:02:37,561 --> 00:02:38,901
Earth again is called the

100
00:02:38,901 --> 00:02:40,251
water cycle.

101
00:02:40,251 --> 00:02:41,561
El Niño does not stop

102
00:02:41,561 --> 00:02:42,961
the water cycle.

103
00:02:42,961 --> 00:02:43,881
It moves where the rain

104
00:02:43,881 --> 00:02:45,171
falls.

105
00:02:46,217 --> 00:02:47,287
With less rain,

106
00:02:47,287 --> 00:02:48,637
forests and peatland in our

107
00:02:48,637 --> 00:02:50,227
region dried out.

108
00:02:50,227 --> 00:02:52,197
Dry land burns easily,

109
00:02:52,197 --> 00:02:53,467
so the fires that started

110
00:02:53,467 --> 00:02:55,817
burned longer and spread further.

111
00:02:55,817 --> 00:02:57,207
On the ninth of October,

112
00:02:57,207 --> 00:02:58,707
Singapore's haze reading,

113
00:02:58,707 --> 00:02:59,967
the PSI,

114
00:02:59,967 --> 00:03:02,267
reached 192.

115
00:03:02,267 --> 00:03:03,877
That is unhealthy.

116
00:03:03,877 --> 00:03:05,457
Remember the smoke particle from

117
00:03:05,457 --> 00:03:06,836
Episode 1?

118
00:03:06,836 --> 00:03:08,896
Even I stayed indoors.

119
00:03:09,541 --> 00:03:11,321
El Niño moves rain around

120
00:03:11,321 --> 00:03:12,381
the world.

121
00:03:12,381 --> 00:03:13,161
In India,

122
00:03:13,161 --> 00:03:14,771
this year's monsoon brought about

123
00:03:14,771 --> 00:03:16,851
one-eighth less rain than normal,

124
00:03:16,851 --> 00:03:18,141
the weakest in over ten

125
00:03:18,141 --> 00:03:19,141
years.

126
00:03:19,141 --> 00:03:20,471
The south and the northeast

127
00:03:20,471 --> 00:03:21,891
were driest.

128
00:03:22,142 --> 00:03:23,202
In the USA,

129
00:03:23,202 --> 00:03:24,172
it works the other way

130
00:03:24,172 --> 00:03:25,792
for some places.

131
00:03:25,792 --> 00:03:26,562
This winter,

132
00:03:26,562 --> 00:03:28,622
scientists expect wetter weather than

133
00:03:28,622 --> 00:03:30,402
usual across the south,

134
00:03:30,402 --> 00:03:32,402
like California and Florida,

135
00:03:32,402 --> 00:03:33,452
and a warmer winter up

136
00:03:33,452 --> 00:03:34,471
north.

137
00:03:34,471 --> 00:03:36,401
So one tired wind changes

138
00:03:36,401 --> 00:03:38,458
the weather in three countries?

139
00:03:38,458 --> 00:03:39,558
Yes.

140
00:03:39,558 --> 00:03:41,068
That is why scientists all

141
00:03:41,068 --> 00:03:42,868
over the world watch it.

142
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,990
Be a weather detective.

143
00:03:44,990 --> 00:03:45,950
Put two cups with the

144
00:03:45,950 --> 00:03:48,130
same amount of water outside:

145
00:03:48,130 --> 00:03:49,260
one in the sun,

146
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:50,770
one in the shade.

147
00:03:50,770 --> 00:03:52,490
Mark the water level.

148
00:03:52,490 --> 00:03:54,280
Check after three days.

149
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,600
Which cup lost more water,

150
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:56,670
and why?

151
00:03:56,670 --> 00:03:58,020
Hint: which one gained more

152
00:03:58,020 --> 00:03:59,190
heat?

153
00:04:00,044 --> 00:04:01,034
Then tell a friend in

154
00:04:01,034 --> 00:04:03,014
India or the USA what

155
00:04:03,014 --> 00:04:04,204
El Niño is doing to

156
00:04:04,204 --> 00:04:05,432
their weather!

157
00:04:05,432 --> 00:04:06,342
See you next time on

158
00:04:06,342 --> 00:04:07,082
TheOneApp,

159
00:04:07,082 --> 00:04:08,372
Explored.

160
00:04:08,585 --> 00:04:10,744
Now you know!
